{"type":"message","id":"6c6e3462","parentId":"581f88d1","timestamp":"2026-04-02T06:11:03.322Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user confirmed the positive/negative examples are acceptable for now. I now have all the information I need to build the complete skill. Let me compile all the interview answers and generate the SKILL.md and supporting files.\n\nSummary of all interview answers:\n\n**Round 1:**\n1. Goal: 分析错因 + 总结解题方法\n2. Trigger phrase: \"讲讲这道数学题\"\n3. Exclusions: 不要直接给答案，要用引导思考、逐步提示\n4. Done criteria: 有错因分析、有引导的问题系列、完成错题图片归档\n\n\n5. OpenClaw as the runtime environment with image reading, document lookup, and file writing capabilities\n6. Need to access reference materials from the Feishu error question archive and previously compiled topic documents, plus any scripts that might be needed for automation\n\nThe output should flow through guided questioning sequences leading into complete solution reasoning, ultimately archived back to the Feishu system.\n\nThe core requirement is starting with a question about where the thinking gets stuck, while explicitly avoiding jumping straight to answers or skipping the guided exploration phase. I'll demonstrate what good mentoring looks like versus poor shortcuts, then generate the complete skill package by creating the necessary folder structure, documenting the skill itself, establishing a quick reference guide, and including test prompts to validate the approach.","thinkingSignature":"4ceea7c6d401c4a88d0942d1d8b2e26a778ba1bc06e5bac00e269a1badf1a717"},{"type":"text","text":"好！开始生成完整的skill包～\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_2o23wlod12rp_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p /Users/edy/.openclaw/workspace/skills/math-tutor/{references,examples,scripts}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":134,"output":321,"cacheRead":61151,"cacheWrite":853,"totalTokens":62459,"cost":{"input":0.0000402,"output":0.000